.TH SDL_CreateWindow 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateWindow \- Create a window with the specified dimensions and flags.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Window * SDL_CreateWindow(const char *title, int w, int h, SDL_WindowFlags flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The window size is a request and may be different than expected based on the desktop layout and window manager policies\[char46] Your application should be prepared to handle a window of any size\[char46]
.PP
.BR flags
may be any of the following OR\(aqd together:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN :
fullscreen window at desktop resolution
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL :
window usable with an OpenGL context
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN :
window is not visible
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS :
no window decoration
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE :
window can be resized
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MINIMIZED :
window is minimized
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MAXIMIZED :
window is maximized
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MOUSE_GRABBED :
window has grabbed mouse focus
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_INPUT_FOCUS :
window has input focus
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MOUSE_FOCUS :
window has mouse focus
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_EXTERNAL :
window not created by SDL
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MODAL :
window is modal
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_HIGH_PIXEL_DENSITY :
window uses high pixel density back buffer if possible
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_MOUSE_CAPTURE :
window has mouse captured (unrelated to MOUSE_GRABBED)
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_ALWAYS_ON_TOP :
window should always be above others
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_UTILITY :
window should be treated as a utility window, not showing in the task bar and window list
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_TOOLTIP :
window should be treated as a tooltip and does not get mouse or keyboard focus, requires a parent window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_POPUP_MENU :
window should be treated as a popup menu, requires a parent window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_KEYBOARD_GRABBED :
window has grabbed keyboard input
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN :
window usable with a Vulkan instance
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_METAL :
window usable with a Metal instance
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_TRANSPARENT :
window with transparent buffer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_WINDOW_NOT_FOCUSABLE :
window should not be focusable
.PP
The
.BR SDL_Window
will be shown if
.BR SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN
is not set\[char46] If hidden at creation time,
.BR SDL_ShowWindow ()
can be used to show it later\[char46]
.PP
On Apple\(aqs macOS, you
.BR must
set the NSHighResolutionCapable Info\[char46]plist property to YES, otherwise you will not receive a High-DPI OpenGL canvas\[char46]
.PP
The window pixel size may differ from its window coordinate size if the window is on a high pixel density display\[char46] Use
.BR SDL_GetWindowSize ()
to query the client area\(aqs size in window coordinates, and
.BR SDL_GetWindowSizeInPixels ()
or
.BR SDL_GetRenderOutputSize ()
to query the drawable size in pixels\[char46] Note that the drawable size can vary after the window is created and should be queried again if you get an
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_PIXEL_SIZE_CHANGED
event\[char46]
.PP
If the window is created with any of the
.BR SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL
or
.BR SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN
flags, then the corresponding LoadLibrary function
.BR "" ( SDL_GL_LoadLibrary
or
.BR SDL_Vulkan_LoadLibrary )
is called and the corresponding UnloadLibrary function is called by
.BR SDL_DestroyWindow ()\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN
is specified and there isn\(aqt a working Vulkan driver,
.BR SDL_CreateWindow ()
will fail, because
.BR SDL_Vulkan_LoadLibrary ()
will fail\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR SDL_WINDOW_METAL
is specified on an OS that does not support Metal,
.BR SDL_CreateWindow ()
will fail\[char46]
.PP
If you intend to use this window with an
.BR SDL_Renderer ,
you should use
.BR SDL_CreateWindowAndRenderer ()
instead of this function, to avoid window flicker\[char46]
.PP
On non-Apple devices, SDL requires you to either not link to the Vulkan loader or link to a dynamic library version\[char46] This limitation may be removed in a future version of SDL\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I title
the title of the window, in UTF-8 encoding\[char46]
.TP
.I w
the width of the window\[char46]
.TP
.I h
the height of the window\[char46]
.TP
.I flags
0, or one or more
.BR SDL_WindowFlags
OR\(aqd together\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the window that was created or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

